1
00:00:00,250 --> 00:00:06,050
The fight pauses at a Choose. The handler holds the rest of the fight as k.

2
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:13,100
To answer, it runs battle itself: the same function a person plays. It needs no model of the game.

3
00:00:13,650 --> 00:00:16,567
For each card it can play, and for ending the turn,

4
00:00:16,567 --> 00:00:20,950
it plays that card on the state, then runs the rest of the fight three times.

5
00:00:22,250 --> 00:00:27,900
Each run has a stack of its own, so it does not use up the dice of the paused fight.

6
00:00:29,650 --> 00:00:36,300
The handler counts the wins. Here every move wins all three. The paused fight has not moved.

7
00:00:36,850 --> 00:00:43,750
With a tie it keeps the first move, Bash. It resumes k with it, and the fight goes on.

8
00:00:44,300 --> 00:00:51,117
On seed 3, the bot answers eleven Chooses with a hundred and sixty-five playouts,

9
00:00:51,117 --> 00:00:53,550
in about a fifth of a second.
